# The stall in a wartime twin: entering it, and getting out with least height lost.
#
#   name TEXT...                   what the lesson is called
#   teaches CLASS                  which class of aircraft it is for
#   stage TEXT...                  a stage, in the order flown
#   do TEXT...                     what to do at this stage
#   until PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE     what ends the stage
#   hold PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT... a band that must hold for the whole stage
#   need PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE TEXT...  what must be true by the stage's end
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/lesson.hpp owns the format.
#
# `stall` is the aeroplane own published stall speed with everything down,
# which `sim::approach_speeds` works out on the way to the threshold speed.
# The height allowed in the recovery is against where the recovery began.
#
# **The stall is called at `stall+25`, not at `stall`.** The published figure
# is the stall with everything down at low level; a clean aeroplane practising
# high breaks well above it, and waiting for the published speed means waiting
# for one that never comes - she breaks, drops, and accelerates away in the
# descent while the lesson watches. The margin is the gap between a published
# low-level figure and where a clean aeroplane at height gives up.

name Stalls in a wartime twin
teaches second-world-war

# **The first sign of the stall is its warning**, where the autopilot's stall
# recovery is held to recovering within this lesson's height (REQUIREMENTS.md
# 4.3). The rules have the warning begin no less than 5 knots or 5% above the
# stall, whichever is more (14 CFR 25.207(c)); this is that least margin, the
# latest a warning may come: the Mosquito stalls at about 95 knots, and 5% of
# that is under 5. It comes after this lesson's entry ends, which is the
# approach to the stall.
warning stall+5

stage Entering the stall
do Close the throttles and hold the height as the speed comes back
do Keep the wings level: a wing drop is what you are avoiding
hold position/h-agl-ft start-150 start+150 Hold the height as the speed comes back
until velocities/vc-kts <= stall+25

stage The recovery
do Move the control column forward to unstall the wing
do Full power as the nose comes down, and level the wings
need position/h-agl-ft >= start-600 Recover with the least height you can
until velocities/vc-kts >= stall+35
